WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.384 --> 00:00:17.085
Three years passed and Sara was still at Miss Minchin's school.

2
00:00:18.665 --> 00:00:22.246
One winter afternoon Sara returned from a drive in her carriage.

3
00:00:23.927 --> 00:00:27.268
As usual she was dressed in her warmest velvets and furs.

4
00:00:31.048 --> 00:00:34.711
A dirty child stood in the stairway leading to the school's kitchen.

5
00:00:35.732 --> 00:00:36.913
Sara smiled at her.

6
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:41.758
"Hello!" The girl looked frightened and darted into the kitchen.

7
00:00:41.778 --> 00:00:47.102
"She must be a servant here," Sara thought.

8
00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:51.847
That evening Sara was telling stories to girls in the schoolroom.

9
00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:57.592
Sara's gift at telling stories was, of course, the greatest power that she had.

10
00:00:58.464 --> 00:01:03.186
When she sat in a circle and began to invent things, her green eyes grew big and began

11
00:01:03.226 --> 00:01:03.727
to shine.

12
00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:08.249
Her cheeks flushed, and her hands fluttered as she told the tale.

13
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.991
The young servant girl came in to tend the fire.

14
00:01:15.693 --> 00:01:18.454
Everyone was listening intently, even Lavinia.

15
00:01:19.514 --> 00:01:22.456
She was very jealous of Sara's ability to tell stories.

16
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.283
"The mermaids swam about in the green water," Sara went on.

17
00:01:28.303 --> 00:01:31.565
"A princess watched them from the shore."

18
00:01:32.845 --> 00:01:36.427
Sara noticed that the servant was working slowly in order to listen.

19
00:01:37.428 --> 00:01:41.010
She swept the hearth in front of the fire, and then swept it again.

20
00:01:42.931 --> 00:01:45.513
Sara began talking louder so the girl could hear.

21
00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:53.828
The servant girl was so interested in the story that she suddenly dropped her dustpan.

22
00:01:53.848 --> 00:01:55.270
"That servant was listening!"

23
00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.371
cried Lavinia as the girl fled.

24
00:01:59.373 --> 00:02:00.975
Sara felt a flash of anger.

25
00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:03.076
"I knew she was listening.

26
00:02:03.457 --> 00:02:04.177
I don't mind."

27
00:02:04.197 --> 00:02:06.520
"Well, you should mind!"

28
00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:07.721
Lavinia said.

29
00:02:09.402 --> 00:02:12.285
That night Sara asked Mariette about the servant girl.

30
00:02:12.305 --> 00:02:16.088
"Her name is Becky," replied Mariette.

31
00:02:17.229 --> 00:02:20.132
"She's the kitchen maid and has to work very hard.

32
00:02:20.896 --> 00:02:26.759
All day long she scrubs floors and cleans windows, and carries heavy things up and down the stairs.

33
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.042
She's very timid, and all the other servants are cruel to her.

34
00:02:31.702 --> 00:02:33.823
They constantly order her around."

35
00:02:33.843 --> 00:02:38.226
"Oh, the poor girl," said Sara.

36
00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:44.289
After Mariette left, Sara thought about Becky for a long time.

37
00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:48.832
She even made up some stories about the hard-working servant girl.

38
00:02:50.252 --> 00:02:55.276
One evening, several weeks later, Sara entered her room and found Becky asleep in her chair.

39
00:02:55.296 --> 00:02:58.278
"Oh!" cried Sara softly.

40
00:02:58.298 --> 00:02:59.999
"There she is!"

41
00:03:04.883 --> 00:03:07.985
Sara sat down, and watched Becky sleep for a moment.

42
00:03:09.326 --> 00:03:12.488
"Miss Minchin would be angry if she found out about this.

43
00:03:12.888 --> 00:03:15.410
But the poor girl looks so tired.

44
00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:18.192
I'll let her sleep for just a few more minutes."

45
00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.504
But then a flaming piece of coal broke off and fell on the hearth.

46
00:03:24.184 --> 00:03:28.068
The sound startled Becky, who opened her eyes with a frightened gasp.

47
00:03:29.149 --> 00:03:30.910
She sprang up and straightened her cap.

48
00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.555
Then she caught sight of Sara and her eyes widened.

49
00:03:36.656 --> 00:03:38.417
Surely Becky would lose her job now!

50
00:03:38.437 --> 00:03:40.979
"Oh, I'm so sorry, miss!"

51
00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:41.880
she cried.

52
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.383
"I didn't mean to fall asleep in your chair.

53
00:03:44.443 --> 00:03:45.724
I just sat down for a minute."

54
00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.421
"It's all right."

55
00:03:50.422 --> 00:03:52.803
Sara laughed and put her hand on Becky's shoulder.

56
00:03:52.823 --> 00:03:56.185
"You were tired.

57
00:03:56.526 --> 00:03:57.586
You couldn't help it."

58
00:03:58.907 --> 00:04:00.348
Becky stared at Sara.

59
00:04:00.969 --> 00:04:04.091
No one had ever spoken to her in such a kind and friendly way.

60
00:04:04.111 --> 00:04:06.552
"Aren't you angry, miss?"

61
00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:07.673
She gasped.

62
00:04:07.693 --> 00:04:11.216
"Aren't you going to tell Miss Minchin?"

63
00:04:11.236 --> 00:04:14.318
"Of course not."

64
00:04:15.178 --> 00:04:17.420
Sara reached out and touched Becky's cheek.

65
00:04:18.636 --> 00:04:20.497
"We're really the same, you and I.

66
00:04:21.097 --> 00:04:22.578
We're both just children.

67
00:04:23.178 --> 00:04:26.339
It's only luck that I'm not you and you're not me."

68
00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.581
Becky didn't know how to respond to this.

69
00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.542
She just said, "Yes, miss."

70
00:04:32.562 --> 00:04:35.223
"Have you finished your work?

71
00:04:35.704 --> 00:04:37.124
Can you stay a few more minutes?"

72
00:04:37.724 --> 00:04:38.465
Sara asked.

73
00:04:38.485 --> 00:04:40.446
"Here, miss?

74
00:04:41.026 --> 00:04:43.207
Me?" "Yes.

75
00:04:43.867 --> 00:04:45.608
I thought you might like a piece of cake."

76
00:04:46.644 --> 00:04:49.406
The next ten minutes seemed like a dream to Becky.

77
00:04:51.387 --> 00:04:54.429
Sara opened a cupboard and gave her a thick slice of cake.

78
00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.832
Sara talked and laughed and asked Becky questions.

79
00:05:01.274 --> 00:05:02.735
Becky began to calm down.

80
00:05:04.216 --> 00:05:07.358
She admired the beautiful pink dress that Sara was wearing.

81
00:05:07.378 --> 00:05:12.662
"Once I saw a princess outside the opera house," said Becky.

82
00:05:12.682 --> 00:05:15.744
"You look just like her in that dress."

83
00:05:17.324 --> 00:05:18.145
Sara laughed.

84
00:05:18.165 --> 00:05:22.407
"I think I'll start pretending to be a princess."

85
00:05:23.788 --> 00:05:27.350
Sara knew that princesses often gave gifts to other people.

86
00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.272
She knew exactly the sort of gift that would please Becky.

87
00:05:31.292 --> 00:05:36.895
"I could tell you some more of my mermaid story every day," offered Sara.

88
00:05:36.915 --> 00:05:40.898
"You mean I could hear it just like the other girls?"

89
00:05:41.338 --> 00:05:42.038
Becky asked.

90
00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:45.020
"Yes," Sara answered.

91
00:05:46.208 --> 00:05:49.833
Becky returned to the kitchen, warm, fed, and happy.

92
00:05:51.134 --> 00:05:53.577
Upstairs in her room, Sara was happy too.

93
00:05:54.538 --> 00:05:56.381
She was only a pretend princess.

94
00:05:57.462 --> 00:06:01.146
But she had found a way to give real gifts to a poor servant girl.
